    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lovely bright detached house with windows on all 4 sides and a south facing back garden.\n\nTo ensure proper spacing of viewings, Casey-Kennedy Estate Agents request that viewers register in advance by email. We will contact you to schedule an exact viewing time. Viewings at this property can also be facilitated by appointment.\n\nThe 14 houses on this end of Meadow Park and on Barton Court to the rear were solidly built by the highly respected Durkans builders in 1991. They are newer than most other houses in the area with an attractive part red brick facade. Number 132 is one of just two detached houses on corner plots adjacent to the green by Nutgrove Way\n\nAccommodation downstairs consists of an entrance hall, spacious living room, kitchen/breakfast room and a further dining room/playroom with French doors to the back garden. There is a guest WC and a storage space under the stairs. Upstairs there are 4 bedrooms and two bathrooms. \n\nThis property is finished with painted walls throughout. There is low maintenance wood effect tiled floors downstairs and in all bathrooms. On the stairs, landing and in all 4 bedrooms there is new carpet. The bathrooms are fitted with new white wash hand basins with cabinets underneath, and new toilets. There is a power supply point over each WHB which should facilitate the fitting of modern lit vanity mirrors. This property is heated by GFCH. It still has the original wood frame double-glazed windows.\n\n132 Meadow Park is conveniently located close to Nutgrove Shopping Centre, Office Park and Retail Park - with an excellent range of shopping, eating and leisure options. It is just 20 minutes walk from Dundrum Town Centre and the LUAS in Dundrum, and 15 minutes walk from Marlay Park.\n\nThis is an excellent family area with an abundance of highly regarded preschools, gaelscoil, primary and secondary schools, and a direct bus route (S6) to UCD. Leisure options abound with Gym Plus, St. Enda`s Park, Marley Park, Ballinteer St. John`s GAA, Leicester Celtic FC and Meadowbrook Leisure Centre all easily accessible.\n\nFreehold property with no annual fee. Vacant and ready for a new owner.\n\nNot rent capped.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Porch - 2.37m (7'9\") x 0.7m (2'4\")\nCovered porch with a tiled floor. Hardwood front door with leaded glazing either side.\n\nHall - 5.7m (18'8\") x 1.95m (6'5\")\nUnder stairs storage. Coving.\n\nLiving room - 5.42m (17'9\") x 3.61m (11'10\")\nLarge window to front. Open fireplace with hardwood mantle flanked by wall lights on both sides. Coving. Centre rose. Virgin Media broadband/TV connection point.\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room - 6.7m (22'0\") x 2.67m (8'9\")\nSouth facing kitchen window over the sink, looking into the back garden. Large window to side. Glazed door to back garden. Single storey kitchen area with potential to add skylights further enhancing the superb natural light in this room. Painted fitted kitchen with white stone counter tops and tiled splashback. Gas boiler.\n\nDining Room / Playroom - 4.53m (14'10\") x 2.9m (9'6\")\nSouth facing French doors to back garden. Large window to side. Coving and centre rose. Useful and flexible space.\n\nGuest WC - 1.74m (5'9\") x 0.76m (2'6\")\nUnder the stairs. Frosted glass window. Vent. WHB. WC. Tiled floor.\n\nLanding - 4.3m (14'1\") x 2.67m (8'9\")\nCarpeted stairs and landing. Lovely and bright with a large window. Attic access hatch. Double doors to tot press (1.5m x 0.6m) with factory insulated hot water cylinder.\n\nFamily bathroom - 2.36m (7'9\") x 1.73m (5'8\")\nFrosted glass window. Full size bathtub with glass shower screen and Triton T90SR electric shower. New WHB with cabinet under. Vanity mirror with shaving light. New white WC.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.35m (14'3\") x 2.96m (9'9\")\nLarge window to front with views across Dublin City. Fitted wardrobes. Door to ensuite.\n\nEnsuite - 2.32m (7'7\") x 1.5m (4'11\")\nFrosted glass window. Full size bathtub with glass shower screen and Triton T90SR electric shower. New WHB with cabinet under. Vanity mirror with shaving light. New white WC.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.41m (11'2\") x 2.92m (9'7\")\nFitted wardrobe. South facing window to rear.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.67m (8'9\") x 2.38m (7'10\")\nWindow to front. Raised platform over the stairs - frequently used as a wardrobe space or for a fitted bed.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.76m (9'1\") x 2.67m (8'9\")\nWindow to rear.\n\nAttic space - 6m (19'8\") x 3m (9'10\")\nPartially finished attic space with flooring and covered rafters. Accessed via hatch from hallway. Max height approximately 1.8m. Originally accessed by an attic ladder, which has since been removed.\n\nBack garden - 11m (36'1\") x 8m (26'3\")\nSouth facing. Access via side passages both sides, back door from kitchen and French doors from playroom. Poorly constructed patio area which will need replacement. Back lawn. Rose bushes in one corner.\n\nFront garden - 9.5m (31'2\") x 8m (26'3\")\nCobblelock off-street parking for two cars. Surrounded by railings and greenery. Facing a large green.\n\nNotice\nIntending purchasers must satisfy themselves as to the accuracy\nof all information and measurements in this listing. Any particulars\nprovided are for guidance only and do not constitute a contract or a part of\none. We do not accept responsibility for any loss or damage arising from\nreliance on this information. Purchasers should seek independent legal and\nprofessional advice."
      },
